### What kind of issue is this?

- [x] React Compiler core (the JS output is incorrect, or your app works incorrectly after optimization)
- [ ] babel-plugin-react-compiler (build issue installing or using the Babel plugin)
- [ ] eslint-plugin-react-hooks (build issue installing or using the eslint plugin)
- [ ] react-compiler-healthcheck (build issue installing or using the healthcheck script)

### Link to repro

https://github.com/aneesijaz/react-compiler-date-bug

### Repro steps

Just run the application. It's a minimal React app created with Vite, and the component is already rendered from App.tsx, so no additional setup is required beyond installing dependencies and starting the dev server.


**Code**
```tsx
import { useEffect, useState } from "react";

export const TimerComponent = () => {
  const [counter, setCounter] = useState(0);
  const time = (new Date()).getTime();

  useEffect(() => {
    const timer = setTimeout(() => setCounter(counter + 1), 1000);
    return () => {
      clearTimeout(timer);
    }
  }, [counter]);

  return (
    <div>{time} - {counter}</div>
  )
}
```

**Result**
<img width="500" height="388" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a376aeb9-54f9-4d2b-b9b9-faacb0be233a" />

**Note:** The code is intentionally minimal to reproduce the issue. I realize it isn't necessarily production-quality code, but I've stripped it down to the smallest example that still demonstrates the problem. Also The code works fine and as expected if not using the compiler.

### How often does this bug happen?

Every time

### What version of React are you using?

19.2.7

### What version of React Compiler are you using?

1.0.0
